# Dependency Discipline

## Required before adding a dependency

1. Clear purpose
2. Prefer mature, maintained projects
3. Inspect license compatibility (final policy via ADR-002 / ADR-003)
4. Avoid unnecessary expansion and duplicate libraries for the same job
5. Pin / lock versions appropriately when implementation exists
6. Review transitive risk and security history
7. Record material dependency decisions

## Prohibited

- Adding a dependency only to save a few lines of code
- Copying third-party code without license compliance review
- Using AGPL/GPL/copyleft in a way that creates unintended project obligations
- Making final license-compatibility claims before ADR-002 and ADR-003 are frozen

Until ADR-003 is FROZEN: do not silently establish lasting dependency policy through code. Propose ADR when the choice is architectural.
